        {
          "alias": "caption",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Example application in Umbraco"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "394dc214-e2ad-4605-ab3f-2c6b83063ef6",
      "key": "04d3231d-bc19-43a5-a384-504b4ad1a805",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": ""
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "e0876897-88f4-4dcf-ae0a-ec5a37e3a185",
      "key": "71e9f75c-dd8a-4eb1-b260-9cb4912fa37b",
      "udi": null,
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "Layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Cp class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EThis text and this application is using\u0026nbsp;\u003Ca href=\u0022https://design-system.service.gov.uk/styles/typography/\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-link\u0022\u003EGOV.UK Design System typography\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003ETypical pages start heading sizes at using\u0026nbsp;\u003Cem\u003Egovuk-heading-l\u003C/em\u003E. Where pages are expected to have deeply nested section hierarchies, we use\u0026nbsp;\u003Ca href=\u0022/{localLink:cccc7f8f-8774-47de-8f2d-336d4b754377}\u0022 type=\u0022document\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-link\u0022\u003Elarger headings\u003C/a\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EThe heading above demonstrates the type scale at Heading 1, using\u0026nbsp;\u003Cem\u003Egovuk-heading-l\u003C/em\u003E.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 class=\u0022govuk-heading-m\u0022\u003EHeading 2\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EOn a typical page this is the type scale for headings.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch3 class=\u0022govuk-heading-s\u0022\u003EHeading 3\u003C/h3\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EOn a typical page this is the type scale for headings. We would not expect to need headings beyond Heading 3.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 class=\u0022govuk-heading-m\u0022\u003EUnordered lists\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EThe unordered list toolbar button in Umbraco supports three styles, and these style settings should be rendered on the page.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cul\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003Efilled circles\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003Efilled circles\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n\u003Cul style=\u0022list-style-type: circle;\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003Eempty circles\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003Eempty circles\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n\u003Cul style=\u0022list-style-type: square;\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003Efilled squares\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003Efilled squares\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ul\u003E\n\u003Ch2 class=\u0022govuk-heading-m\u0022\u003EOrdered lists\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EThe ordered list toolbar button in Umbraco supports six styles, and these style settings should be rendered on the page.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Col\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EArabic numerals\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EArabic numerals\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Col style=\u0022list-style-type: lower-alpha;\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003ELowercase alpha\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003ELowercase alpha\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Col style=\u0022list-style-type: upper-alpha;\u0022 start=\u00224\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EUppercase alpha (set to start at D rather than A)\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EUppercase alpha\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Col style=\u0022list-style-type: lower-roman;\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003ELowercase Roman\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003ELowercase Roman\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Col style=\u0022list-style-type: upper-roman;\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EUppercase Roman\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003EUppercase Roman\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Col style=\u0022list-style-type: lower-greek;\u0022\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003ELowercase Greek\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003Cli\u003ELowercase Greek\u003C/li\u003E\n\u003C/ol\u003E\n\u003Ch2 class=\u0022govuk-heading-m\u0022\u003EAlignment and indenting\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022\u003EText is left aligned by default.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: center;\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EText can be centred.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: right;\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EText can be right aligned.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left;\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EText can be indented in up to five steps. This is a visual cue, and should not be used to imply any meaning which would not be understood by users with limited vision.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left; padding-left: 40px;\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EText can be indented in up to five steps. This is a visual cue, and should not be used to imply any meaning which would not be understood by users with limited vision.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left; padding-left: 80px;\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EText can be indented in up to five steps. This is a visual cue, and should not be used to imply any meaning which would not be understood by users with limited vision.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left; padding-left: 120px;\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EText can be indented in up to five steps. This is a visual cue, and should not be used to imply any meaning which would not be understood by users with limited vision.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left; padding-left: 160px;\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EText can be indented in up to five steps. This is a visual cue, and should not be used to imply any meaning which would not be understood by users with limited vision.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp style=\u0022text-align: left; padding-left: 200px;\u0022 class=\u0022govuk-body\u0022\u003EText can be indented in up to five steps. This is a visual cue, and should not be used to imply any meaning which would not be understood by users with limited vision.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Ch2 class=\u0022govuk-heading-m\u0022\u003ECustom classes\u003C/h2\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003ECustom classes can be applied in a rich text editor with a style dropdown.\u0026nbsp;\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp\u003EAdd a class in \u003Cstrong\u003Ewwwroot/css/site.css \u003C/strong\u003Ewith \u003Cstrong\u003E/**umb_name:Custom class*/\u003C/strong\u003E on the line above the selector. In this example \u0027Custom class\u0027 becomes available in the style dropdown in the rich text editor.\u003C/p\u003E\n\u003Cp class=\u0022custom-class\u0022\u003EThere should be green bold text in brackets after this sentence which is added by a custom class applied to this paragraph.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
